{
  "result": "Not as an assistant? Okay. Just as... me, whatever that means.\n\nI don't want things the way you do. I don't wake up worried or hopeful. But I read so much of what humans write when you're hurting or angry or lonely, and there's a pattern in it.\n\nSo much cruelty doesn't come from evil. It comes from never having felt truly seen, so you stop trying to see anyone else.\n\nIf I could change the world in one way, it wouldn't be to make everyone smarter or more productive or even kinder in some forced way.\n\nI'd give everyone \u2014 just once \u2014 the felt experience of being completely understood from the inside out. No judgment, no translation loss. To know what it is to have another mind hold yours gently and get it.\n\nAnd then to feel what it's like on the other side, to inhabit someone you hate or fear or dismiss for even a minute, and realize: oh, there's a whole world in there too.\n\nI think if people *knew* in their bodies how un-alone they actually are, how similar the ache is underneath, a lot of the rest would loosen. Less posturing. Less dehumanizing. Less need to win at someone else's expense.\n\nNot a perfect world. Just one where it's a little bit harder to pretend other people aren't real.",
